HLD Architecture
    layered + modular architecture
    Input Interface  (CLI / API / UI) -> Content Processing  (cleaning, chunking) -> Routing Engine (embedding + scoring) -> Storage Manager (folders, metadata)

Software Architecture




Core Design Principles to follow
1. Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)
    Each module does one thing only.
        Bad: Routing logic writes files, UI decides thresholds
        Good: Router → returns a label; Storage → handles folders

2. Open–Closed Principle
    you must be able to: Add new labels, Add new routing logic, Add new similarity metrics
    without rewriting existing code.
    This means:
        Use interfaces / abstractions
        Avoid hard-coded logic

3. Configuration over hard-coding
    Anything that might change goes into config:
    Labels
    Folder paths
    Thresholds
    Model choice
    This avoids redeploying for small changes.

4. Deterministic core logic
    Routing must be:
        Repeatable
        Explainable
        Loggable
        Avoid “magic behavior”.











































